TASK_29_EV_CHARGING_NETWORK_PLANNER
EV Charging Network Planner
Project Overview

The EV Charging Network Planner is a data-driven infrastructure planning system designed to support the expansion of electric vehicle (EV) charging networks. The project analyzes charging station performance, identifies underserved regions, predicts future charging demand, and recommends optimal locations for new charging stations. It combines data analytics, SQL, machine learning, geographic analysis, and Power BI dashboards to assist infrastructure leadership in making strategic investment decisions.

Business Problem

With the rapid growth of electric vehicles, existing charging infrastructure faces challenges such as uneven coverage, congestion, long waiting times, and inefficient resource allocation. The objective of this project is to identify infrastructure gaps, prioritize expansion opportunities, and optimize investment planning for future EV charging networks.

Project Objectives
Analyze the existing EV charging infrastructure.
Identify underserved regions and coverage gaps.
Forecast future charging demand.
Build machine learning models for expansion recommendations.
Perform geographic analysis using interactive maps.
Develop Power BI dashboards for strategic decision-making.
Recommend locations for new charging stations and station upgrades.
